selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#per-locus-categories-and-the-custom-legend\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Per-locus categories and the custom legend<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#per-locus-categories-and-the-custom-legend\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>The <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">category</span></code> column lets you group loci in the legend:</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#mixed-genome-builds\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Mixed genome builds<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#mixed-genome-builds\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>If your files were generated on different reference panels, pycmplot\ncan lift over hg18 and hg19 coordinates to hg38 before plotting.\nSupply the per-file builds via a comma-separated <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">--build</span></code> list in\nthe same order as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">--sum_stats</span></code>:</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#automatic-gene-annotation\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Automatic gene annotation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#automatic-gene-annotation\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>By default, significant hits are annotated by SNP ID.\nAdd <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">--annotate</span> <span class=\"pre\">gene</span></code> (case insensitive) to label each lead SNP with its nearest\ngene, and optionally <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">--label_col</span> <span class=\"pre\">top_gene</span></code> to control which\ncolumn from the hits table is used as the label. We will build on\nthe <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#cli-tut-multi-track-highlight\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">Multi-track</span></a> base above.</p><p>Let\u2019s also add a line tracing the highlighted positions across\ntracks using <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">--highlight_line</span></code>.</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#highlighting\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Highlighting<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#highlighting\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p><strong>Highlight, and add plot title and significant/suggestive lines to the base above</strong></p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#cli-equivalents\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">CLI equivalents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#cli-equivalents\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>Everything above has a CLI equivalent.  A representative one-liner:</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#troubleshooting\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Troubleshooting<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#troubleshooting\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2>", "a[href=\"changelog.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Changelog<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#changelog\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h1><p>All notable changes to <strong>pycmplot</strong> are documented here.</p><p>The format is based on <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/\">Keep a Changelog</a>\nand this project adheres to <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://semver.org/\">Semantic Versioning</a>.</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#the-hits-overlay-tsv\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">The hits overlay TSV<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#the-hits-overlay-tsv\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>When caching is enabled, the loader writes the hits table to a\ngroup-scoped TSV that <strong>you\u2019re expected to hand-edit</strong>.  The path is:</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#setup-a-synthetic-dataset\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Setup: a synthetic dataset<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#setup-a-synthetic-dataset\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>Every CLI invocation below assumes six synthetic sumstats files on\ndisk (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">trait{1..6}.tsv.gz</span></code>). Download the python script used for benchmark\n<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://github.com/esohkevin/pycmplot/blob/main/benchmark/generate_sumstats.py\">here</a> and run it as shown below.</p><p>The code below generates six sumstats, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">triat1</span></code> to <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">trait6</span></code>, each containing\n1 million SNPs. Traits 1 to 3 are in hg19 coordinate while traits 4 to 6 are\nin hg38 coordinate. All the files are gzipped and saved in the folder <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">data</span></code>.\nThe <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">--targets</span> <span class=\"pre\">auto</span></code> option injects 6 significant loci on chr3, chr6, chr11,\nchr13, chr18, and chr20 in all sumstats, 2 significant loci specific to hg19 sumstats\n(in chr2 and chr15) and 2 significant loci specific to hg38 sumstats (in chr12 and chr16).\nThese are actuall <strong>body height</strong> significant loci pulled from <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/gwas/efotraits/OBA_VT0001253\">GWAS Catalog</a>.</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#the-cli-mental-model\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">The CLI mental model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#the-cli-mental-model\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>Every <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pycmplot</span></code> invocation performs the same three steps internally\n\u2014 column resolution, data loading (+ optional liftover, lead extraction,\nhits-table construction), and rendering.  From the CLI you don\u2019t have\nto think about them separately: one command runs the whole pipeline\nand writes the output image(s) plus a locus summary TSV.</p><p><strong>The canonical minimum invocation is:</strong></p>", "a[href=\"#indices-and-tables\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Indices and tables<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#indices-and-tables\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#next-steps\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Next steps<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#next-steps\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#pycmplot\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pycmplot<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#pycmplot\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h1><p><strong>pycmplot</strong> is a Python package for generating multi-track circular and linear\nManhattan plots from GWAS summary statistics. It accepts any number of per-variant\nsummary statistic files \u2014 GWAS, selection scans (iHS, FST, XP-EHH), or any\ncolumn-delimited p-value table \u2014 and produces publication-ready Manhattan plots\nwith automatic gene annotation, lead-SNP extraction, and optional hg19 \u2192 hg38\ncoordinate liftover.</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#per-locus-highlight-colours\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Per-locus highlight colours<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#per-locus-highlight-colours\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>Set the <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">highlight_color</span></code> column on any row to a matplotlib-parseable\ncolour (name, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">#rrggbb</span></code> hex, or an <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(r,</span> <span class=\"pre\">g,</span> <span class=\"pre\">b)</span></code> tuple):</p>", "a[href=\"#key-features\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Key features<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#key-features\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#gui-editor-for-the-hits-overlay\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">GUI editor for the hits overlay<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#gui-editor-for-the-hits-overlay\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>If hand-editing the <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">hits.&lt;group&gt;.tsv</span></code> in a text editor feels\nawkward \u2014 especially picking colours by typing hex codes \u2014 pycmplot\nships an optional browser-based editor.  Install the extra and launch\nit against your cache directory:</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#caching-and-warm-resume\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Caching and warm resume<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#caching-and-warm-resume\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>Loading is the expensive step (I/O + trim + liftover + lead\nextraction).  Turn on caching and every re-run of the same\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(files,</span> <span class=\"pre\">parameters)</span></code> combination completes in milliseconds:</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#multi-panel-canvas\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Multi-panel canvas<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#multi-panel-canvas\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>Multi-panel canvases \u2014 where each panel is its own stacked linear (or\ncircular) sub-plot \u2014 are a <strong>Python API</strong> feature.  The CLI produces\none figure per invocation; if you need multiple sumstats groups laid\nout on the same canvas (e.g. Hb on top, MCV on bottom, sharing a\ntitle and legend), use the notebook workflow described in\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"python_api_tutorial.html#python-api-tutorial\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">Python API Tutorial</span></a> under \u201cMulti-panel canvas\u201d.  Every cache\nfile, hits overlay, per-locus colour, and category legend is\n<em>group-scoped</em> under both interfaces, so two panels with different\nsumstats never clobber each other\u2019s artefacts.</p>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">CLI Tutorial<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#cli-tutorial\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h1><p>This tutorial is an end-to-end walkthrough of every user-facing feature\nin <strong>pycmplot</strong> from the <em>command line</em>, working from the same synthetic\ndataset throughout so that every command is directly copy-pasteable.\nIt\u2019s longer and more granular than <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"quickstart.html#quickstart\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">Quickstart</span></a> \u2014 read the\nquickstart first if you just want to see the shape of the CLI in a page.</p><p>Looking for the equivalent Python-API walkthrough?  See\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"python_api_tutorial.html#python-api-tutorial\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">Python API Tutorial</span></a> \u2014 it covers the same features using the\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pcm.prep</span></code> / <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pcm.load</span></code> / <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pcm.linear</span></code> / <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pcm.circular</span></code>\nfunctions in a runnable Jupyter notebook.</p>", "a[href=\"#contents\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Contents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#contents\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2>", "a[href=\"cli_tutorial.html#qq-plots-and-compute-pvals\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">QQ plots and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">compute_pvals</span></code><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#qq-plots-and-compute-pvals\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\uf0c1</a></h2><p>The loader normally skips materialising the full sorted p-value\narray (~80 MB per track at 10 M variants) because most users never\ndraw a QQ plot.  The CLI <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">--qq_plot</span></code> flag turns that computation on\nautomatically \u2014 you never need to think about the underlying\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">compute_pvals</span></code> parameter:</p><p>Note, circular Manhattan is always generated by default.</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }
            link.classList.add('has-tippy');
            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 500, interactive: true, theme: 'light-border',

            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
